menu "Advanced Klipper tuning"
  help
    Compatibility and timing workarounds applied by Happy Hare when Klipper starts.
    These settings are shared by all MMU units. Keep the defaults unless troubleshooting
    a specific problem; timing workarounds do not fix wiring or overloaded hardware.

  config PARAM_UPDATE_TRSYNC
    boolint "Increase homing synchronization timeout?"
    default 0
    help
      Raise Klipper's TRSYNC_TIMEOUT to at least 0.05 seconds. This can help with
      timing failures during homing, particularly with CANbus-connected MCUs.
      It does not resolve every "Timer too close" error. The change is applied in
      memory at startup without editing Klipper files and affects Klipper globally.
      Default 0 leaves Klipper's timeout unchanged.

  config PARAM_UPDATE_BIT_MAX_TIME
    boolint "Relax NeoPixel timing tolerance?"
    default 1
    help
      Raise Klipper's NeoPixel BIT_MAX_TIME to at least 0.000030 seconds (30 us).
      This workaround can help older LEDs that produce "Unable to obtain
      'neopixel_result' response" errors in klippy.log.
      It is applied in memory at startup without editing Klipper files and affects
      all Klipper NeoPixels. Default 1 preserves Happy Hare's shipped configuration;
      set to 0 to leave Klipper's timing unchanged.

  config PARAM_UPDATE_AHT10_COMMANDS
    boolint "Use AHT30-compatible commands with the legacy AHT10 driver?"
    default 0
    help
      Compatibility workaround for the BTT ViViD AHT30 sensor on older Klipper
      versions without native support. Configure the sensor using the AHT10 driver
      and enable this to replace that driver's command table at startup.
      This affects all sensors using that driver, not just the MMU sensor.
      Leave disabled when using native sensor support. Default 0 leaves the
      Klipper command table unchanged.

endmenu
